Router guard capability gating. Add RouteMeta capability. Import useSystemStore, SystemCapabilities type. Guard:
```ts
if (to.meta.capability && auth.isAuthenticated) {
  const system=useSystemStore()
  await system.load()
  if (system.loaded && !system.enabled(to.meta.capability)) {
     return { name:'chat', query: { blocked: String(to.name ?? '') } }
  }
}
```
But `system.load()` catches errors and sets loaded false; if fails, allow.
- Add meta to routes: workflows: workflows, agents: agents, tasks: tasks, knowledge: knowledge.
- `loaded` exposed.
- Could show toast in ChatView if `route.query.blocked`. Add in ChatView onMounted or watch: ElMessage.info(`${label}能力将在...`). Maybe not necessary. But direct URL redirect without explanation is confusing. Add `blocked` handling in ChatView:
```ts
const blockedLabel: Record<string,string> = {agents:'智能体',tasks:'任务',knowledge:'知识库',workflows:'工作流'}
onMounted(() => { const blocked=route.query.blocked; if (typeof blocked==='string' && blockedLabel[blocked]) { ElMessage.info(`${...}能力当前关闭...`); void router.replace({query:{...route.query, blocked:undefined}}) } })
```
But this runs before system load maybe; okay. Maybe skip toast to reduce scope. Add simple.

